A||||4||operator64||Mobil oil is Smoking||||1||
Z||000000||operator64||09-25-2001||02:57 PM||||   Changed my oil this weekend and changed to Mobil from Trop-Artic.  The old oil had 2200 miles on it caused a little smoke from time to time nothing to bad, after changing the oil to Mobil i could have killed mosquitoes for a living. I kept with the same grade 10-40 , now i have changed it back to Trop-artic and all is good. Quite odd that a brand could do something so different in just 50 miles of driving.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||09-25-2001||04:18 PM||||What engine do you have? I have the 4 cyl, and my engine seems happiest with Mobil one. I wouldn't think there would be enough difference between oils to make one smoke and another not smoke. Also what is Trop-Artic oil? I haven't heard of it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||Rick 88||09-25-2001||04:29 PM||||How many miles are on your engine? Synthetic oil flows very well and will find leaks and worn engine parts easily. Worn valve guides and rings will cause more smoke with synthetic oil than regular oil.<P>Rick 88||||reg||5
Z||000003||operator64||09-25-2001||04:53 PM||||   I have the 2.5 4 cylinder with 91,000 miles. I did not use a synthetic this was straigh Mobil 10/40. If i had used a synthetic i could understand it happening.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||09-25-2001||07:44 PM||||I used to say oil is oil, as long as both oils have the same API service rating and viscosity they are the same. Well I ran Mobil in my truck once.....only once. The oil got so thin when it warmed up that the oil pressure would drop drasticly. The engine had around 100000 miles on it at the time. I switched back to whatever other brand I was using at that time and my oil pressure was back up to normal.<P> I'm a mechanic for a Toyota Dealer and all we use is Toyota oil. I have been told it is made by Mobil but to higher standards. In fact in Japan Toyota specifies 20,000 mile oil changes. I've been running Toyota oil in my Ford service van and I haven't changed the oil since 100,000, it's at 128,000 now. I just add oil when it's low. Shhh!! Don't tell the boss!<P>On a side note, a guy at work told me about this 'smokless oil' he uses. Used car dealers use it to help sell cars that burn oil. Aparently it doesn't make any smoke when it burns, and it really does work. Only $6/quart. Imagine the new car owners dismay when they get their car back from it's first oil change and it's smoking like crazy!||||reg||1
